Maintainer: Somanos Sar <somanos.sar@drumee.com>
Standards-Version: 2.9.7
Homepage: https://drumee.org

Package: drumee-server-pod
# Architecture: any, not all. The payload is a node_modules tree carrying 18 compiled
# .node addons, every one linux-x64 (@img/sharp-linux-x64,
# @msgpackr-extract/msgpackr-extract-linux-x64, @parcel/watcher-linux-x64-*). Under
# `all` that amd64 build installed cleanly on arm64 and then failed at require() — no
# dpkg error, no startup error until the first call into sharp or msgpackr. See
# docs/distribution.md §9.1. `any` means one build per architecture, which is honest:
# apt now refuses on an architecture nobody has built rather than installing something
# that cannot work.
Architecture: any
# drumee-node-runtime supplies pm2, which /usr/sbin/drumee invokes by name and
# which nothing previously installed: a fresh install came up with every package
# "installed ok" and nothing serving, failing with "pm2: command not found" in the
# journal. Debian ships no pm2 package, so the pinned set in drumee-node-runtime is
# the only versioned source for it. Unversioned on purpose — the exact version
# belongs to release-manifest.yaml, and check-packaging.sh forbids naming a
# component version in a control file.
#
# It pulls in nodejs (>= 22) transitively, which Trixie cannot satisfy on its own
# (it ships 20). scripts/debian.sh configures NodeSource before installing, so
# the documented path resolves. A bare `apt install drumee` on a stock Trixie now
# fails at install time instead of installing cleanly and never starting.
#
# drumee-schemas and drumee-static are deliberately NOT here.
#
# schemas pulls mariadb-server, which the container design puts in its own container
# (the official mariadb:11.8 image) — an app role carrying a database server is the
# monolith again. static is 181 MB of assets belonging to the web role. Both were
# declared because on a single box every component was installed anyway.
#
# Safe to drop because this postinst needs neither at configure time: it guards its use
# of the rendered environment (`if [ -f /etc/drumee/drumee.sh ]`) and its patch step
# (`if [ -x $patch ]`), and the DB work those patches do happens at server startup, not
# at dpkg time. A complete native install is guaranteed by the `drumee` metapackage,
# which pins every component exactly.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nginx, redis-server, redis, node-redis, inotify-tools, graphicsmagick, libgraphicsmagick1-dev, poppler-utils, libreoffice, dcraw, curl, p7zip-full, ffmpeg, drumee-node-runtime
Description: Drumee Server
